Huayu wrote:

> This may be a stupid question, considering I haven't been playing
> this game long and still suck at it, but...couldn't you just wish for
> a scroll of charging? Or can you only use one scroll of charging on
> the wand of wishes, so that would effectively waste a potential wish?

When you find a wand of wishing, the first thing to wish for is "2
blessed scrolls of charging" (if you don't have one yet).

Then you identify the wand, just in case it was (0,1) when you found it
and has now become (0,0). You don't want to risk it turning to dust with
your second zap.

When it's not (0,0) yet, zap it for wishes until it is empty (0,0). Then
read one of your blessed scrolls of charging. This will recharge it to
the maximum value for wands of wishing (3). You'll now have a wand of
wishing (1,3). Zap three times for three more wishes.

Now #adjust your wand to the inventory slot "z", and keep trying to zap
the wand by pressing "zz". Eventually, you will get a last wish from the
wand, and the wand will turn to dust (there's only a small chance per
zap that it will grant you a last wish).

Don't think of using that second blessed scroll of charging: you can
only recharge a wand of wishing once. Trying again will blow up the
wand.

